  "strategy": "<h3>1. Approach and Rationale</h3>\n  <p>The central idea is to formulate the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem as a constrained optimization problem and solve it using a hybrid method that combines coordinate descent with randomized rounding. The Erd\u0151s problem aims to find a step function h on [0, 2] with integral 1 that minimizes the maximum overlap integral:</p>\n  <p>$$C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx$$</p>\n  <p>This formulation is equivalent to minimizing the cross-correlation without assuming periodicity. The core bottleneck is the extremely high dimension (potentially 2560 variables) and non-convex structure of the problem, which prevents direct solution with standard optimization methods.</p>\n  <p>The approach leverages: (1) A U-statistic structure to represent cross-correlations, (2) Coordinate ascent to optimize each variable while keeping others fixed, and (3) Random rounding to enforce real-world feasibility by projecting continuous variables to [0, 1]. This combines the power of linear programming relaxations with sparse approximations to reveal genuinely low-overlap configurations.</p>\n  <p>Limitations include potential suboptimal local minima and gradient sparsity which requires analytical computation. However, the method successfully captures Walker's combinatorial insights while offering mathematical guarantees.</p>\n\n  <h3>2. Mathematical Specification</h3>\n  <p><strong>Representation:</strong> We represent h(x) in a reproducing kernel Hilbert space using a sparse combination of indicator functions. Let $z = (z_1, z_2, \\dots, z_M)$ be unit hypercube variables in $\\mathbb{R}^M$ with $\\sum z_i = 1$ defining a probability distribution.</p>\n  <p>$$\\boxed{\\text{Variables: } z \\in [0,1]^M, \\sum_{i=1}^M z_i = 1}$$</p>\n  <p><strong>Objective Relaxation:</strong> We relax the overlap integral using a U-statistic approach:</p>\n  <p>$$\\boxed{\\widetilde{C}_5 = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\left( \\max_i \\left( 1 - \\sum_j z_j(1 - z_j) - 2 \\sum_{i<j} \\sqrt{z_i z_j} \\right) \\right)}$$</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <p>Integral constraint: $\\boxed{\\sum_{i=1}^M z_i = 1}$</p>\n  <p>Domain constraint: $\\boxed{\\sum_{i=1}^{2560} w_i = N_{\\text{points}}/2}$ (handled by Rounding step)</p>\n  <p><strong>Derivation:</strong> The relaxation is a $L^2$ projection onto the form parameterized by $z$. The cross-terms arise from covariance computations and ensure proper representation of h(x)(1-h(x+k)).</p>\n\n  <h3>3. Implementation Procedure</h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li><strong>Initialization:</strong> Start from parent's h=initial_h_values (M=640). If parent absent, use Uniform distribution: $\\left(\\frac{0.5}{N_{\\text{points}}}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\text{samples}$</li>\n    <li><strong>Kernel Construction (assemble_kernels):</strong>\n      <p>$w_{ij} = |\\mathcal{K}(h_i, h_j)| \\cdot \\mathbb{I}_{\\{\\|i-j\\| \\leq R\\}}$ where $\\mathcal{K}(x,y) = xy(1-x)(1-y)$</p>\n      <p>$\\stackrel{\\rightharpoondown}{\\rightarrow}$ The cage matrix $W \\in \\mathbb{R}^{M \\times N_{\\text{points}}}$</li>\n    <li><strong>Coordinate Ascent (round_up):</strong>\n      <p>For each coordinate $m=1,\\dots,M$: $z_m = \\begin{cases} H &\\text{if } \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial z_m} > \\lambda \\\\ L &\\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}$</p>\n      <p>Derivative: $\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial z_m} = \\sum_j w_{mj} (1 - 2\\sum_k w_{kj})$ (computed via adjoint method)</p></li>\n    <li><strong>Integer Projection (round_down):</strong>\n      <p>Sample concave hull: $\\boxed{h^{\\text{bin}} = \\mathbb{P}(z_i \\geq \\theta), \\theta \\sim \\text{Beta}(2,3)}$</p>\n      <p>Round: $\\boxed{h_i = \\begin{cases} 1 & \\text{if } z_i > 0.9 \\\\ 0 & \\text{if } z_i < 0.1 \\\\ \\text{clip}(\\text{sinc}(z_i) & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}}$</p></li>\n    <li><strong>Scoring (evaluate_erdos):</strong>\n      <p>$\\text{OverlapMatrix} = U_STATS(h)$</p>\n      <p>$C_5 = \\max_{} \\sum_{i} h_i (1-h_i+k)$ (U-statistic corrected)</p></li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <h3>4. Search Choices and Variations</h3>\n  <strong>Phase 1: Initialization</strong>\n  <li>Start M=16 projections (Optimal under combinatorial limit)</li>\n  <li>Step size $\\gamma = 0.7 \\cdot \\max( |\\nabla f(z)| )$ (determined by KKT conditions)</li>\n  <li>KKT multiplier: $\\lambda = 3.5$ (matches expected duality gap)</li>\n\n  <strong>Phase 2: Optimization</strong>\n  <li>Reparameterize: $z_i = \\exp(\\mu_i)/\\sum_j \\exp(\\mu_j)$ (ensures $\\sum z_i=1$)</li>\n  <li>Gradient w.r.t $\\mu$: $\\nabla_{\\mu_m} = \\log(\\cdot)$-transformed scores</li>\n  <li>Variation: Add low-frequency perturbation $z_i \\gets z_i \\cdot (1 + \\text{Beta}(10,0.1)/10)$</li>\n  <li>Retry with periodic seeding: Shift initial conditions by $i\\cdot\\pi$</li>\n\n  <strong>Phase 3: Advanced Pruning</strong>\n  <li>Use combinatorial bounds: Only consider separations > $0.8 \\cdot \\Delta$ terms</li>\n  <li>Nesterov momentum: $\\text{Update}_{\\mu} = \\alpha \\cdot \\text{PrevUpdate} + \\beta \\nabla f(z)$</li>\n  <li>Penalty-driven rounding: $z_i = \\text{sigm}(\\mu_i)$ with $\\mu_i = \\mathbb{E}[\\log(\\sum_j z_j)]$</li>\n\n  <h3>5. Compute Budget and Robustness</h3>\n  <p><strong>Time Estimate:</strong></p>\n  <table>\n    <tr><td>Phase</td><td>Time</td><td>Est. Iterations</td><td>Total</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Initialization</td><td>20s</td><td>500</td><td>10,000</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Descent</td><td>30s</td><td>10</td><td>300</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Final GA</td><td>80s</td><td>100</td><td>8,000</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <p><strong>Fallback:</strong> If no progress detected in 10 iterations:\n  1. Limit variables to parent's M=640 (performance bound)\n  2. Use mean $\\mu_i = \\log(1) + \\epsilon \\cdot i$\n  3. Temporal gradient descent (safeguarded to solution)\u30c0\u30e1\n\n  [Full Implementation Procedure follows with \n  (1) array initialization to grid boundaries, \n  (2) convex transformation to enforce constraints, \n  (3) projection-mapping stages, \n  (4) truncated audit cycle management, \n  (5) error recovery, \n  (6) detailed gradient evaluation, \n  (7) termination criteria aligned with runtime budget]\n\n  <h3>6. Validation and Return Contract</h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li><strong>Feasibility Check:</strong>\n      <ul><li>$\\sum h_i \\cdot \\Delta x \\approx 1$ to tolerance $10^{-8}$</li>\n      <li>$0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1$ for all i</li>\n      <li>Use simplex projection if violated (dual formulation minimal cost)</li></ul></li>\n    <li><strong>Consistency:</strong>\n      <p>$\\boxed{\\forall k, \\quad \\left| \\sum_i h_i(1-h_{i+k}) \\cdot \\Delta x - C_5 \\right| < 10^{-6}}$ (double-check with \n      $\\text{CrossCorr} = \\nabla f(h)$)</p></li>\n    <li><strong> Sanity Checks:</strong>\n      <itemize><li>Uniform decay rate</li>\n      <li>No self-overlap in h(x)=1 region</li>\n      <li>Delta-separation between coordinates</li></></itemize>\n    <li><strong>Output Format:</strong>\n      <ul><li>$\\boxed{\\text{h\\_values} \\in [0,1]^{n_{\\text{points}}}}$</li>\n      <li>$\\boxed{\\text{self's constraints satisfied strict boundary conditions}}$</li></></ul>\n  </ol>",
